  "worked_solution": "We require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot x+(-4)\\cdot y \\\\ (-3)\\cdot x+1\\cdot y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Notice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4y \\\\ -3x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation  $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
